{#
    Pushes server-confirmed measurement events into the GTM dataLayer, then
    tells the server the browser really did it.

    Expects `analytics_events` — a list of {id, name, payload} from
    App\Service\Analytics\AnalyticsEventFlusher::pendingFor().

    The acknowledgement is the point: this page is reached from a link in an
    e-mail, and mail scanners fetch such links without running JavaScript. If
    the server marked the events delivered at render time, a scanner would eat
    the conversion and the customer's own click would push nothing. Only a
    browser that actually ran this script confirms, so anything that cannot
    run it leaves the event pending for the next real visit.

    The push itself happens regardless of cookie consent, and that is correct:
    dataLayer is a plain JavaScript array in the visitor's own page. Pushing to
    it neither stores anything on the device nor sends anything anywhere, so
    ZEK § 89 odst. 3 — which governs storing on / reading from terminal
    equipment — does not reach it. What consent gates is the GTM *tags* that
    read the dataLayer and transmit, and those are held by Consent Mode v2
    (components/_gtm_head.html.twig).
#}
{% if gtm_container_id and analytics_events is defined and analytics_events|length > 0 %}
    <script>
        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
        {% for event in analytics_events %}
        window.dataLayer.push({{ { 'event': event.name }|merge(event.payload)|json_encode|raw }});
        {% endfor %}

        /* keepalive so the confirmation survives the customer navigating away
           in the same instant; a failure just leaves the event pending. */
        try {
            fetch({{ path('public_analytics_ack')|json_encode|raw }}, {
                method: 'POST',
                keepalive: true,
                headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body: JSON.stringify({ ids: {{ analytics_events|map(e => e.id)|json_encode|raw }} })
            }).catch(function () {});
        } catch (e) {}
    </script>
{% endif %}
